Package: CompositeIndexAudit
Title: Pre-Fitting Algebraic Classification of Composite Indices Entered
    Alongside Their Own Components
Version: 0.34.0
Authors@R: person("Shuqiong", "Su", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "sushq@example.org")
Description: Composite indices are routinely entered into a regression
    together with the very measurements they are computed from. Whether the
    index coefficient then estimates anything depends on the pair (index,
    base model), and that can be decided before fitting, from the registered
    expression alone. The package parses an index expression, matches its
    components to the base model columns on a five-field term identity
    (variable, transformation, log base, units, encoding), classifies the
    pair into one of four classes or an explicit non-classification state,
    and returns the coefficient map linking the two parameterisations when
    one exists. A fitted-model entry point reads the design matrix, aliased
    columns, family, offset and weights off a 'glm', 'lm', 'svyglm',
    'coxph' or 'survreg' object. The classification is symbolic; the
    numerical layer verifies it and never proves it.
